Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.10,0:00:04.57,English,en-0,0,0,0,,{\q2}The troop-strength table has two columns: one tracks only the regiments present
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.10,0:00:04.71,Chinese,zh-0,0,0,0,,{\q2}兵力表分成两列：一列只追踪起点那批兵团，另
Dialogue: 1,0:00:04.57,0:00:08.88,English,en-1,0,0,0,,{\q2}at the start; the other retains all relevant armies actually held under that
Dialogue: 2,0:00:04.71,0:00:09.11,Chinese,zh-1,0,0,0,,{\q2}一列保留这个方案实际拥有的全部相关军队。
Dialogue: 1,0:00:08.88,0:00:09.16,English,en-2,0,0,0,,{\q2}plan.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:09.11,0:00:13.67,Chinese,zh-2,0,0,0,,{\q2}新增一人，不能自动抹平原兵团的缺员；源军
Dialogue: 1,0:00:09.16,0:00:14.31,English,en-3,0,0,0,,{\q2}One additional person cannot automatically cancel out a shortfall in the original regiments.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:13.67,0:00:18.01,Chinese,zh-3,0,0,0,,{\q2}在合并后消失，也不能当作整支军队死亡。
Dialogue: 1,0:00:14.31,0:00:18.78,English,en-4,0,0,0,,{\q2}Nor does a source army disappearing after a merge mean the entire army has died.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:18.01,0:00:21.22,Chinese,zh-4,0,0,0,,{\q2}人数、身份和组织变化一起看
Dialogue: 1,0:00:18.78,0:00:24.26,English,en-5,0,0,0,,{\q2}Counts, identities, and organizational changes must be read together to see where the troops went.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:21.22,0:00:24.18,Chinese,zh-5,0,0,0,,{\q2}，才知道兵究竟去了哪里。
